// What this account has already announced, so a milestone is announced once and not once per
// level-up afterwards. See general/scripts/milestones.rs2.
//
// A 99 and a max cape need no mark: stat_base never falls, so "this level-up took the skill to
// exactly 99" and "this 99 was the twenty-third" are each true on exactly one level-up. Total
// level and combat level are different - both can rise by more than one in a single advance, so
// asking "is it exactly 2000" would miss the player who went from 1999 to 2001. These hold the
// highest threshold already announced and the test is "past it and not yet marked".

// The highest total-level milestone announced: 0, then 1000, 1500, 2000, 2277.
[milestone_total_mark]
scope=perm
protect=no

// 1 once combat level 126 has been announced.
[milestone_combat_mark]
scope=perm
protect=no

// 1 once this account has been announced as a new arrival.
[milestone_welcomed]
scope=perm
protect=no

// 1 once a staff command has given this account progress it did not earn - ::setstat,
// ::advancestat and ::minme in the engine, and ~sl, ~hunter, ~droptest and every quest debugproc
// in content (general/scripts/milestones.rs2 lists them and says why the content ones cannot be
// caught in the engine). From then on nothing this account does is announced as a milestone.
//
// WHY THE WHOLE ACCOUNT AND NOT THE ONE SKILL. The moment any level is set by hand, the total
// level, the combat level and the max cape are all fabricated too - they are sums of that skill.
// A per-skill flag would have to suppress those three for the whole account anyway, so the only
// thing it would buy is announcing a 99 in a skill that was not the one that was set, on an
// account that has already shown it will set them. And a per-skill flag has nothing to say at all
// about the quest list or the collection log, which the content doors reach.
//
// AND WHY IT IS PERMANENT. The announcement says a player got somewhere. A cheated base does not
// stop being cheated because experience was earned on top of it later. The engine says so once, in
// the chatbox, when it first sets this - a staff member who set a stat to test something and wants
// their own milestones back can clear it with ::setvar milestone_cheated 0.
[milestone_cheated]
scope=perm
protect=no
